  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "title",
      "value": "Spellweaver Armor"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "json": [
        {
          "text": "When most think of an archmage, they often think of a long beard and flowing robes. \n\nWhile not archmage armor, the "
        },
        {
          "text": "Spellweaver Armor",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": " is the battle standard for the "
        },
        {
          "text": "Wizard Council's",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": " magi, used by many of their adept wizards and is inspired by the archmage's armor itself. \n\nThe armor itself is as strong as a knight's chainmail, and while wearing it, I have "
        },
        {
          "text": "significantly more mana and mana regeneration",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ". \n\nIt allows "
        },
        {
          "text": "levitation",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": " "
        },
        {
          "text": "(double tap space to toggle)",
          "italic": true
        },
        {
          "text": ". \n\nFinally, it has a replenishing bank of three defensive runes that will "
        },
        {
          "text": "reflect projectiles",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ". Each rune goes dormant after reflecting a projectile, and will come back online after a brief recharge period of a few seconds, allowing it to reflect another projectile."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
